            'Under late-century SSP5–8.5, baseline F1,F2 andF3 effective-infection dates shift−4.81,−7.85 and−14.51 days relative to flowering; F1 symptoms shift−3.66 days, with a three-model range−6.24 to−1.82. Mean flowering–BBCH85 duration changes only+0.12 days, with both shorter and longer model-specific windows. Upper-three-leaf HAD deficit increases from6.50 to9.12 days per unit nominal LAI: a2.62-day change, model range1.28–4.39 and spatial Monte Carlo standard error0.33 (Figure5a–b). The greater deficit therefore accompanies earlier disease relative to grain filling without a consistent shortening of that window.',
