            'The field comparisons qualify this mechanism at each scale. German station holdouts support retained development under known sowing and realized weather. Broad flag-stage intervals and sparse soft-dough evidence constrain the additional leaf and grain-fill windows. Fully nested selection removes shared nuisance estimation from disease-inner evaluation without improving the chosen setting or resolving weak identification. Grouped uncertainty distinguishes the poorly resolved BASF timing comparison from the poorer Corteva source-numbered-leaf result. Ambiguous leaf identity and retrospective reuse remain observation limitations; they cannot be repaired by interpreting simulated infection dates as measured events.',
